<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer - provisions to be below 36 mln Sfr.</title>
<headline>Sulzer - provisions to be below 36 mln Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>RUETI, Switzerland 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Sulzer official, who declined to be named, said 1996 provisions for job cuts at weaving machinery unit Sulzer Reuti should not exceed about 36 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>&quot;It shouldn't be more than three dozen million in 1996 provisions (for the job cuts),&quot; a Sulzer executive told Reuters.</p>
<p>He declined to be more specific.</p>
<p>Sulzer today said it planned to cut 950 out of 3,200 jobs by the end of 1997 at the Sulzer Rueti division due to ongoing recession and weak growth in global markets for weaving machinery.</p>
<p>Sulzer Rueti group president Helmut Pirchl said earlier that provisions for major job cuts through 1997 would be taken mainly in 1996 and will lower Sulzer group net profit.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
